<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's real wages fall five pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Hungary's real wages fall five pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's monthly average real wages fell five percent in 1996, the Central Statistical Office (KSH) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY AVERAGE MONTHLY WAGE IN 1996</p>
<p>			Blue collar    White collar     All</p>
<p>			 employees	employees	employees</p>
<p>Gross average</p>
<p>  wage (forint)    35,305	    62,309	   46,837</p>
<p>Net average</p>
<p>  wage (forint)    24,833	    38,207	   30,544</p>
<p>Net average</p>
<p>  wage rise (pct)  18.2		16.3	     17.4</p>
<p>NOTE: The figures released include the business sphere, and also the agricultural sector and public institutions.</p>
<p>The KSH earlier said that monthly average wages in the business sector fell 3.6 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>Average inflation was 23.6 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>Comparative figures were not available.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
